{"name":"Fantasy Console Sky","hex":"#29adff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fantasy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["That which comes from one's imagination or the act of imagining things.","The literary genre generally dealing with themes of magic and the supernatural, imaginary worlds and creatures, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To conceive (something) mentally; to imagine.\n To fantasize about (something).","To conceive (something) mentally; to imagine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fantasy"},{"term":"console","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stand-alone cabinet designed to stand on the floor; especially, one integrated with home entertainment equipment, such as a TV or stereo system.","A desk-like cabinet, table, or stand upon which controls, instruments, and displays are mounted."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To comfort (someone) in a time of grief, disappointment, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/console"},{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Video game console emulator","blocks":[{"text":"A video game console emulator is a type of emulator that allows a computing device to emulate a video game console's hardware and play its games on the emulating platform. More often than not, emulators carry additional features that surpass limitations of the original hardware, such as broader controller compatibility, timescale control, easier access to memory modifications, and unlocking of gameplay features. Emulators are also a useful tool in the development process of homebrew demos and the creation of new games for older, discontinued, or rare consoles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/RetroArch_running_Dandy_%28Atari_800%29.png/330px-RetroArch_running_Dandy_%28Atari_800%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Video_game_console_emulator","wikidata":"Q1196126"},{"title":"Fantasy","blocks":[{"text":"Fantasy is a genre of speculative fiction that involves supernatural or magical elements, often including completely imaginary realms and creatures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/The_Whirlwind_Seizes_the_Wreath.jpg/330px-The_Whirlwind_Seizes_the_Wreath.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fantasy","wikidata":"Q132311"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","wikidata":"Q527"},{"title":"Sky blue","blocks":[{"text":"Sky blue refers to a collection of shades comparable to that of a clear daytime sky. Typically it is a shade of cyan or light teal, though some iterations are closer to light azure or light blue. The term is attested from 1681. A 1585 translation of Nicolas de Nicolay's 1576 Les navigations, peregrinations et voyages faicts en la Turquie includes \"the tulbant [turban] of the merchant must be skie coloured\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Shades_of_light_blue.png/330px-Shades_of_light_blue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_blue","wikidata":"Q373160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/CelesteClassic.png/500px-CelesteClassic.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/CelesteClassic.png/500px-CelesteClassic.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The PICO-8 prototype of Celeste","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACelesteClassic.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Li_Song-Skeleton_Fantasy_Show.jpg/500px-Li_Song-Skeleton_Fantasy_Show.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Li_Song-Skeleton_Fantasy_Show.jpg/1280px-Li_Song-Skeleton_Fantasy_Show.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Li_Song-Skeleton_Fantasy_Show.jpg/500px-Li_Song-Skeleton_Fantasy_Show.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Painting Skeleton Fantasy Show (骷髏幻戲圖) by Li Song (1190–1264)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALi_Song-Skeleton_Fantasy_Show.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/The_violet_fairy_book_%281906%29_%2814730388126%29.jpg/500px-The_violet_fairy_book_%281906%29_%2814730388126%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/The_violet_fairy_book_%281906%29_%2814730388126%29.jpg/1280px-The_violet_fairy_book_%281906%29_%2814730388126%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik